uick correct decisions, calm in crisis, excellent attention, concern for others, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. B's strengths: conscientious, stress handling, weather assessment, computer skills, but weak memory for numbers, nasty remarks, grumpy. A's weaknesses: unorganized, no stress resilience, unfriendly, unhealthy eating.\n\nWe need to decide if C remains best. The panel hasn't covered all criteria fully, but we can argue that C's decision quality and calmness are top, and his attention skills address attention, and his concern for others helps crew cooperation despite communication issues. D's decision quality is adequate but not as strong as C's quick correct decisions; also D's crew cooperation concerns are similar or perhaps worse (arrogant, weak leadership). So C remains best.\n\nThus we will state we continue to recommend Candidate C, explaining why despite communication issues, his decision quality, calmness, attention, and concern for others outweigh B's memory issues and D's arrogance.\n\nWe need to reference Agent 2's point about B's weak memory for numbers and Agent 1's info about D's arrogance and weak leadership. Also reference our own earlier note about C's quick correct decisions, calmness, attention, concern for others.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I remain with Candidate C...\" etc.\n\nMETADATA_JSON: vote \"Candidate C\"."}
